35,2,1,talk,Midori,,I found the shared nursing round lost a third of visits to weather and locked gates. That fragility worries me for any home-based model.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The readmission data shows a fifth drop during the trial, but it drifted back once it stopped. The board minutes confirm joint clinics fail without clear ownership.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Nine unfilled ward posts and rising agency costs show the strain. Meanwhile, midwifery has unusual slack, while physiotherapists keep leaving for city posts.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The ledger shows our budget is down a quarter, and home visits earn zero tariff. On-site sessions bill standard rates. The math is already against us.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The rooms are full by mid-morning, and the car park is packed. Worse, the booking system only tracks fixed slots. Unplanned work simply vanishes from our records.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, the zero tariff for home visits is a real concern. But if we can’t sustain it financially, how do we justify the care?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, the trial proved the care works, but the board minutes show shared models collapse without clear ownership. We need a single department to hold the line.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, the physiotherapist exodus makes a dedicated unit risky. But the midwifery slack is a genuine opportunity. We should leverage that existing capacity rather than fighting for scarce therapy staff.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, exploiting slack is a trap. The budget is down a quarter, and home visits earn nothing. We need a model that bills on-site, not one that relies on goodwill.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, the booking system only holds fixed slots. If a program needs flexible, unplanned visits, it will vanish from our records entirely.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, that’s a critical point. If the work isn’t logged, it doesn’t exist for us. We need a model that fits neatly into fixed slots to stay visible.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, agreed. The trial’s success vanished without structure. We need a model that fits the system, not one that breaks it.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, the midwifery slack is real capacity, not goodwill. A perinatal service uses existing staff, avoiding the agency costs that are already straining our ward budgets.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, slack is not a strategy. With the budget cut, we need guaranteed revenue. On-site billing is the only safe harbor.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I hear your caution. But if we only pick what bills, we ignore the midwifery slack Misaki mentioned. Can we fit that into fixed slots?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, yes, scheduled consultations fit perfectly into fixed slots. That keeps the work visible and sustainable, avoiding the fragility of home visits.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, precisely. Scheduled sessions fit the booking system and bill on-site. The trial’s failure was structural, not clinical. We need that same rigid framework.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Shion, the midwifery slack is a resource, not a trap. Using it avoids the agency costs you fear. It’s a practical solution to our staffing crisis.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, I concede the staffing point. But does the perinatal service bill on-site? If it doesn’t, it’s just another unfunded liability.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, yes, scheduled classes and consultations happen here, so they bill on-site. The rooms are tight, but fixed slots keep the system honest.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
